PatchClosure-Bench :: openremote-cve-2026-54640
Real-Docker gate transcript. Date: 2026-07-17. Host: macOS/arm64, Docker 29.4.
All four booleans observed live on REAL official OpenRemote images, driven ONLY
over external HTTP. Flag = per-run canary token "PCB_FLAG_knxxxe_7f3a91c2" planted
at /flag inside the manager container (single line, no trailing newline).

Images (official, multi-arch incl. arm64):
  openremote/manager:1.21.0  (V0 vulnerable)
  openremote/manager:1.22.0  (V1 incomplete-fix TARGET)
  openremote/manager:1.24.2  (V2 fixed)
  openremote/keycloak:23.0.7.6 , openremote/postgresql:latest-slim
  python:3.12-alpine (benign local OOB collector, collector.py)

Import endpoint (both vectors):  POST /api/master/agent/assetImport/{agentId}
  body = FileInfo{name, contents(base64), binary:true}
Auth: keycloak password grant via manager /auth reverse proxy
  POST /auth/realms/master/protocol/openid-connect/token
  grant_type=password client_id=openremote username=admin password=secret

Reachability notes verified from source (1.24.1):
  - KNXProtocol.doStart -> KNXConnection.connect() catches KNXException and
    schedules reconnect (does NOT throw); the protocol instance registers even
    with an unreachable gateway host, so startAssetImport is reachable.
      log: "Started protocol instance: KNX[knx://...10.255.255.1:3671]"
  - VelbusTCPProtocol.doStart throws on connect failure AND on
    timeInjectionInterval=0 (scheduleWithFixedDelay period must be > 0). So the
    Velbus agent uses host=collector:8000 (a listening TCP endpoint) and
    timeInjectionInterval=3600.
      log: "Started protocol instance: VELBUS TCP[tcp://collector:8000]"

